{"seq":6,"at":"2026-10-21","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0765"},"reason":"Proofread (reasons in the entries above / the batch report).","by":"enrich batch 169","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-enrich/enrich-report/a0525-a0969.md","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",30],["-","The"],["+","A"],["=",1],["-","card's"],["+","classic"],["=",1],["-","question"],["+","example"],["=",1],["-","concerns"],["+","is"],["=",1140],["+"," The name itself goes back to the French chemist Michel Eugène Chevreul, who in 1815 called the substance found in gallstones cholestérine, from the Greek for bile and solid."],["=",152]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",30],["-","Die"],["+","Ein"],["=",1],["-","Frage"],["+","klassisches"],["=",1],["-","der"],["+","Beispiel"],["=",1],["-","Karte"],["+","ist"],["=",1],["-","betrifft "],["=",1089],["+"," Der Name selbst geht auf den französischen Chemiker Michel Eugène Chevreul zurück, der den in Gallensteinen gefundenen Stoff 1815 „cholestérine“ nannte, nach den griechischen Wörtern für Galle und fest."],["=",152]]}],"hash":"b6fd858fe373"},
